# --- byte-compiled / env -------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store

# --- never commit model weights -----------------------------------------
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.gguf
# ANCHORED. Unanchored, these match at any depth, and git does not descend into
# an excluded directory, so results/published/<arm>/models/ could not be
# re-included by any rule below. Same defect as the `plots/` line under it.
/hf_cache/
/models/

# --- benchmark output ----------------------------------------------------
# Raw runs are large and machine-specific. Only curated, committed-on-purpose
# results under results/published/ enter git.
results/*
!results/published/
!results/.gitkeep
*.ncu-rep
*.nsys-rep
*.qdrep

# --- plots ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated from the CSVs on every run, so tracking them means binary churn
# on each sweep. publish_results.sh copies the relevant ones into
# results/published/<label>/ so a kept result set carries its own figures.
# Anchored. Unanchored `plots/` matches at ANY depth, so it silently swallowed
# results/published/<arm>/plots/*.png on every publish: publish_results.sh copies
# the figures in and logs "included N figure(s)", then git add drops every one.
# Zero .png files are tracked under results/published/ across all ten arms.
/plots/

# --- traces --------------------------------------------------------------
# Captured routing histograms ARE committed: they are kilobytes and they are
# the point of the project. Raw router logits are not.
traces/raw/
*.logits.npz

# --- triton / cuda caches ------------------------------------------------
.triton/
*.cubin
*.ptx
*.so

# --- stray notebooks ------------------------------------------------------
# An empty Untitled.ipynb was committed by accident in 66d4d53 and lived in the
# repo root for a week. Jupyter names them this by default, so the default name
# is the one to catch.
Untitled*.ipynb

# --- pod session ------------------------------------------------------------
# scripts/pod_session.sh creates this before its own preflight runs, and an
# untracked entry here makes the tree dirty, which run_all.sh then stamps onto
# every row it writes as git_dirty. 76.7% of the canonical pool is already
# unusable that way.
/session/

# --- raw evidence under results/published/ ---------------------------------
# THE RULE THAT DROPPED THE EVIDENCE, twice. `/plots/` above is anchored
# because an unanchored `plots/` matched at ANY depth and swallowed every
# figure a publish copied into results/published/<arm>/plots/. The extension
# rules below it (*.ptx, *.cubin, *.nsys-rep, *.ncu-rep, *.qdrep) still match
# at any depth, so results/published/<arm>/ptx/kernel.ptx was ignored on
# exactly the same terms: `git add` said nothing, the C3 PTX evidence survives
# only as tarballs, and pod_session P9 had to remind the operator to tar the
# dumps because git would not take them.
#
# results/published/ is the one place in this repo where those files ARE the
# artefact, so they are re-included here. ORDER MATTERS: a negation only wins
# when it comes after the pattern it undoes, which is why this block is last.
# A PARENT MATTERS MORE: git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so no
# `!` under it can ever fire. That is why `models/` and `hf_cache/` above are
# anchored to the repo root rather than left to match at any depth; an arm
# directory called models/ would otherwise be unrecoverable from here.
!results/published/**/*.ptx
!results/published/**/*.cubin
!results/published/**/*.ncu-rep
!results/published/**/*.nsys-rep
!results/published/**/*.qdrep
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT re-included: *.safetensors, *.bin, *.pt, *.pth, *.gguf.
# Those are weight formats, a single mixtral shard is gigabytes, and "never
# commit model weights" is worth more than the one raw dump per year that
# happens to use a weight extension. Exfil that one as a .tar.gz, which this
# block leaves committable.
